    "measure": "Each rate is 100 times the number employed in the indicated population divided by the size of that population. The denominator includes everyone in that population aged 15 or older. Employment covers work for pay or profit, including workers temporarily absent from their jobs.",
    "groups": "The female rate uses the female population aged 15 or older and the male rate uses the male population aged 15 or older. The total uses the full population aged 15 or older and comes directly from its own published series.",
    "interpretation": "Differences between rates are measured in percentage points. These annual estimates include national observations and modeled values. The release supplies no observation-level imputation flags. Population coverage, country definitions and methods can affect comparisons. The publisher cautions against ranking countries on imputed estimates."
